From 178dd2c295d4c54cf114eadc2641ad7e121c3d80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nyasha <nmushambi@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:45:20 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: tegra132: add the GPU throttle level to the heavy
 throttle

soctherm_throt_cfg_parse() requires nvidia,gpu-throt-level and rejects the
whole throttle config without it ('throttle-cfg: heavy: no throt prop or
invalid prop'), so on Tegra132 boards nothing ever throttled and the only
thermal protection left was the hardware thermtrip power cut. On the Nexus 9
that cut power under sustained CPU+GPU load (boot reason cold_boot).
Tegra124 already sets both levels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132.dtsi
index cd6aacb9f..2c1a7a915 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132.dtsi
@@ -959,6 +959,7 @@ throttle-cfgs {
 			throttle_heavy: heavy {
 				nvidia,priority = <100>;
 				nvidia,cpu-throt-level = <TEGRA_SOCTHERM_THROT_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+				nvidia,gpu-throt-level = <TEGRA_SOCTHERM_THROT_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 
 				#cooling-cells = <2>;
 			};
-- 
2.56.0

